  "question": {
    "text": "An aeroplane flying horizontally <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>&nbsp;above the ground is observed at an elevation of <math><msup><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math> and after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> seconds the elevation is observed to be <math><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math>. The uniform speed of the aeroplane (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>km</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math>), is"
  },
